      <p class="answer">Get people and pets clear, stay away from any wire, then call. Everything else can wait for the crew.</p>
      <p>Professional help makes sense whenever a tree or limb is touching a structure, hanging over somewhere people walk, leaning more than it used to, or is too big to cut safely from the ground. A chainsaw on a loaded trunk is the most common way homeowners get hurt after a storm.</p>
